{
  "paper_summary": "This paper presents Sun-as-a-star analyses of spatially integrated H\u03b1 spectra to investigate various solar active events, such as flares, filament eruptions, and off-limb prominence eruptions. The primary dataset is from the Solar Dynamics Doppler Imager (SDDI) on SMART at Hida Observatory, with complementary data from GOES soft X-ray measurements, SOHO/LASCO coronagraph images, and SDO/AIA multi-wavelength imagery. These instruments are used to identify event timing, verify CME occurrence, and interpret event scenarios for events between November 2016 and May 2021.",
